{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And I cast it into the fire, and this calf came out.</b> All that has been mentioned until now in the matter of the calf, our Rabbis of blessed memory call the first calf, and this account which is Aaron's they call the second calf. And this is what they said: the deed of the first calf is read and translated, and the second is read but not translated. What is the reason? Because of Aaron's honor. Thus did the Rabbis of blessed memory expound at the end of [ tractate ] Megillah." "<b>And the explanation of the matter</b> is that even though two mentions were recorded above — one in the Torah's narrative, ״ויעשהו עגל מסכה״, and one in the Holy One's narration to Moses, ״עשו להם עגל מסכה״ — all of it is reckoned as one matter, and all of it is read and translated. But here, in Aaron's account, which he himself recounts concerning his own sin with his own mouth — had this been translated, it would not have been to his honor. And furthermore, he used in it the expression ״ויצא״, that is, it came out on its own; and by this the prosecuting counsel could argue: since it came out on its own, it had material substance."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:06:28.569033383Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}